[h1]Quick Deal Indicator[/h1]

Never miss a deal the AI would accept again.

A small badge on the [b]Diplomacy[/b] button (bottom right, above End Turn) shows how many factions currently have a [b]Quick Deal[/b] with a [i]Deal chance[/i] of 0 or more — the deals the AI will accept.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Count badge[/b] on the Diplomacy button: number of factions with at least one acceptable deal (0 when there are none).
[*][b]Hover the badge[/b]: it lights up and its tooltip lists every acceptable deal, as [i]Faction - Deal type (chance)[/i].
[*][b]Click the badge[/b]: diplomacy opens directly on the Quick Deal view (Known Factions list with the Deal chance column), on the first deal type that has an acceptable deal.
[*]All deal types: non-aggression pact, trade agreement, military access, defensive and military alliance, peace, and vassal / tributary / confederation when your faction can use them.
[*]Exactly the game's own numbers: the mod asks the game for the same score the diplomacy screen shows.
[*]Always up to date: refreshed when you load a campaign, at the start of your turn, and during your turn after army moves, battles, settlements changing hands, diplomatic events and whenever a panel closes.
[*]In your game's language: all text comes from the game itself (tested in English and French).
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Save-game compatible: enable or disable at any time.
[*]Doesn't replace any vanilla file, so it works alongside other mods, including UI mods.
[/list]

[h2]Something wrong?[/h2]
Bug reports, source code and a step-by-step debugging guide:
[url=https://github.com/emmanuel-h/wh3-quick-deal-indicator]github.com/emmanuel-h/wh3-quick-deal-indicator[/url]

Please include your game version, your other mods and what you did when it happened.

